# ============================================================================
# 0trust receiving wallet — identity pin
# ============================================================================
# The SHA-256 of the extended PUBLIC key that receives customer payments.
#
# The key itself is not here, and must never be. An xpub exposes the wallet's
# entire balance and transaction history to anyone holding it, permanently,
# and it cannot be rotated without moving the funds — so it lives in
# WALLET_BTC in /etc/0trust/api.env on the control plane and nowhere else.
#
# A digest gives up none of that and still catches the failure this project
# treats as its worst: a truncated, mistyped or wrong-account key derives
# perfectly valid addresses belonging to somebody else. Invoices never settle,
# customers pay into a wallet the operator cannot spend from, and every health
# check stays green the whole time. There is no error to notice.
#
# So scripts/check-wallet.sh compares whatever key it is handed against this
# line, and scripts/install.sh and scripts/preflight.sh both refuse a key that
# is not the one recorded here.
#
# Recorded 2026-08-25: a BIP84 account zpub (native segwit, bc1q… addresses).
#
# Running this deployment against a different wallet:
#     ./scripts/check-wallet.sh --pin <your-zpub>    # rewrites the line below
# Deleting the line disables the comparison entirely.
#
sha256:ac5863cea1b0c134fab8740a50247f1a8e3e6c03c049eaaf01d42377f4bcf484
